From: David Lang <david@lang.hm>
Subject: [PATCH] ucode: update to Git HEAD (2026-10-28) from openwrt master

Carry openwrt.git master's package/utils/ucode/Makefile verbatim
(3e6064bbbf6f "ucode: update to Git HEAD (2026-10-28)", ucode-lang/ucode
dfc64d41) on top of OPENWRT_VER 41a1874c, which ships ucode f7c2b97a
(2025-12-01). Needed for the nl80211 event fixes:

  520d9f4c nl80211: fix waitfor() busy-spinning on non-blocking event socket
  e6bf0a9d nl80211: fix listener.request() dropping multicast events
  05328e33 nl80211: fix memory leak in waitfor() on repeated matching events
  e4a16597 nl80211: don't report waitfor() match on event parse failure
  0bfb7b97 nl80211: recover the event listener from receive buffer overruns
  395cfeea (and follow-ups in the same series)

520d9f4c is the fix for the `iwinfo <if> scan` hang (100% CPU busy-spin)
seen on the SCALE 23x (March 2026) APs.

The four local patches of 41a1874c are dropped, as master does:
  100-add-include-for-older-kernels     upstream as 3d999b21f4ba
  110-uloop-allow-reusing-the-existing-environment  upstream as f8c2d64f546c
  111-uloop-add-optional-setup-callback-to-process  superseded upstream by
      1ed0e1b405fe (pass a function instead of the path); nothing in the
      41a1874c tree calls uloop.process()
  121-fs-add-read_nb-method-for-non-blocking-reads  not upstream; nothing
      in the 41a1874c tree uses fs read_nb()

Note PKG_ABI_VERSION changes 20230711 -> 20261009 (struct uc_vm grew,
hostapd embeds it), so every libucode user (hostapd/wpad, rpcd, uhttpd,
udebug, uclient, ucode-mod-*) is rebuilt against the new headers; the
image is built from source so that is automatic.

The first full mt798x build found source-compatibility requirements
in the old libucode users (three packages); carry their minimal upstream fixes with this
ucode update so they are also toggled off with it:
  udebug 6726e98: explicitly include <fcntl.h> (new ucode public headers
      no longer supply it indirectly, after ucode 9ba6ea14).
  uhttpd ca796d7: a switch default for the new STATUS_BREAK VM status
      (otherwise -Werror=switch fails the build).
  rpcd a6c6b63: the same STATUS_BREAK switch default in rpcd's ucode.c.
Both are upstream backports, not toolchain workarounds.

Drop this patch when OPENWRT_VER contains 3e6064bbbf6f (or newer ucode).

The deciding drop signal is the on-device behavioral test
(wifi_scan_spin_test.sh TESTS=A) passing on an image built without this
patch (SKIP_SOURCE_PATCHES=002), not the presence of that commit. The
known OpenWrt landing of both 520d9f4c and 0bfb7b97 is a4e922953c8d.
---
